  "Question": "The remainder when the product \\(1492 \\cdot 1776 \\cdot 1812 \\cdot 1996\\) is divided by \\(5\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\)",
    "C": "\\(2\\)",
    "D": "\\(3\\)",
    "E": "\\(4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Only the ones digits of the factors affect the ones digit of their product. To see why, split each factor into its ones digit and a multiple of \\(10\\). When multiplying, every contribution involving one of those multiples is itself a multiple of \\(10\\).\n\nThe ones digits of the four factors are \\(2,6,2,6\\), and\n\\[\n2\\cdot6\\cdot2\\cdot6=144.\n\\]\nThus the original product ends in \\(4\\). Subtracting \\(4\\) leaves a multiple of \\(10\\), which is divisible by \\(5\\). Since \\(4<5\\), the required remainder is \\(4\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
